0092 another-programs-drag-ends-ours: Wayland: a drag handed to the compositor carries the application's own type (the clipboard's), so one entering a window without it is another program's and the one handed over has ended, though its source was never told (Hyprland, after a drop on an XWayland window or when the target dies at the drop): its source and image are let go of and its window told (FileDropEvent::Ended) before the other is taken, never taken for it coming back; a source let go of before neither answers nor ends the drag under way, and the type that marks it holds nothing

